  {
    "council_member": "Bryan Madden",
    "council_position": "President",
    "organization": "Valley of the Sun YMCA",
    "website": "http://valleyymca.org",
    "about": {
      "about_url": "http://valleyymca.org/our-mission/donate/",
      "mission": "",
      "description": "The Valley of the Sun YMCA needs your help to provide financial assistance to the most vulnerable populations in our community. Donate today!",
      "raw_text": "When you give to the YMCA, you’re not just making a donation; you’re creating real impact, opportunity, and hope across Arizona. Your generosity fuels programs that uplift our neighbors, helping individuals and families build safer, stronger futures and reach their full potential. As a nonprofit organization, we rely on the kindness of donors like you to make this mission possible. Together, we can build a more connected, supportive, and resilient community, one person, one family at a time.\n\nThank you for helping us make a lasting difference.\n\nCommunity Connector:You help people who feel isolated find connection, belonging, and support through YMCA programs.\n\nChildcare Supporter:You make affordable, high-qualitychildcareavailable for working families and children.\n\nHousing Pathway Provider:You help young adults access safe,stable transitional housingas they move toward independence.\n\nFood Security Champion:You help reducefood insecurityby ensuring access to nutritious meals.\n\nEmployment Opportunity Builder:You supportjob readiness and workforce programsthat help people gain skills and employment.\n\nChild Water Safety Advocate:You help protect children throughwater safety education and drowning prevention.\n\nQuestions about giving? Emailgive@vosymca.orgor call602.212.5114. Learn about other ways to givehere.\n\nWe offer accessible, high-quality child care that working parents can rely on. With your support, children are welcomed into safe, enriching environments where they can grow socially, emotionally, and academically. Our programs give families peace of mind, knowing their kids are learning and thriving even when life gets busy or unpredictable.\n\nMany young adults in our community face unstable living situations due to aging out of foster care, family conflict, or financial hardship. Your donation helps us provide transitional housing to members of your community. With wraparound support and life skills training, residents can focus on education, employment, and building a future with confidence and dignity.\n\nWe’re committed to meeting people where they are, and that often starts with basic needs. Your gift helps stock our food pantries, provide hot meals, and connect individuals to employment resources and training. Whether someone is recovering from job loss or facing a temporary setback, the Y is here to offer a hand up and a path forward.\n\nDrowning is one of the leading causes of death for children in Arizona, and we believe every child deserves to feel confident and safe in the water. Your donation allows us to offer free and low-cost swim lessons and water safety education to families across our communities. These programs save lives, build confidence, and open up a world of safe, healthy fun.\n\nAt the Y, no one is turned away because of age, background, or ability to pay. Thanks to your generosity, we’re able to offer a wide range of inclusive programs from youth sports and after-school clubs to senior wellness and support groups. These activities foster connection, boost mental and physical health, and create a true sense of belonging for everyone involved.",
      "meta_description": "The Y is for EVERYONE. The Valley of the Sun YMCA is not only one of the oldest nonprofits in the state of Arizona, but we are also one of the largest."
    },
