      "mission": "",
      "description": "Serving the entire state of Arizona, we are fueled and guided by our mission to grant life-changing wishes for children with critical illnesses, every day.",
      "raw_text": "We strive to create an inclusive and diverse office that incorporates teamwork, communication and strategic leadership.\n\nWe are lucky to have incredible corporate and organizational leadership through our Board of Directors.\n\nWe are always on the lookout for great talent who share our passion for the Make-A-Wish mission.\n\nDiscover everything from the wishes we grant to the incredible supporters who make them possible.\n\nSee the many ways you can help grant wishes by shopping, local promotions, and more.\n\nSee the latest updates about Make-A-Wish Arizona plus recent wishes and upcoming events near you.\n\nMake-A-Wish Arizona proudly celebrates a historic milestone in its 45-year history, granting a record-breaking 476 life-changing wishes, the most in the chapter’s history.\n\nWatch the videocelebrating our chapter's 45th Anniverary and the more than 8,500 life-changing wishes granted.\n\nThe beloved Chris Greicius statue returned to Make-A-Wish Arizona at its new home at the Parsons Wish House in Scottsdale, Arizona. Linda Pauling, Chris Greicius' mother and Make-A-Wish Co-Founder, welcomed the statue back.Read the article here!\n\nTour the Parsons Wish House in Scottsdale to learn how Make-A-Wish began in Arizona and see our historic timeline featuring 45 years of wishes!\n\nMake-A-Wish Arizona Board of Directors\n\nMake-A-Wish Arizona Phoenix Wishmakers Council\n\nMake-A-Wish Arizona Southern Arizona Wishmakers Council\n\nConnect with our communications team to access news releases, background information and recent news about Make-A-Wish Arizona.\n\nJessica HaagSenior Director of PR and Marketing2901 North 78th StreetScottsdale, AZ 85251Direct Line: 602-343-9434Email: jhaag@arizona.wish.org\n\nWatch Brendan's wish to have a puppy!\n\nSee more ways how you can get involved with our chapter and help grant wishes!\n\nMake-A-Wish Arizona is a 501(c)(3) non-profit, tax-exempt Arizona corporation. Every dollar our chapter receives aids us in our mission to grant wishes of children with critical illnesses. Our financial statements have been audited annually and past statements are available for review upon request.\n\nAt Make-A-Wish, our mission is to create life-changing wishes for children with critical illnesses. Our families and medical professionals share with us that a wish becomes an important part of the healing process, helping children manage, and even overcome, their illnesses.\n\nLike the world around us, we continue to see an increase in the average cost of a wish. We have also expanded our community outreach and partnership work so that we can be good stewards of your funds, monitor our program ratio, and grow the number of wish kids we reach year-over-year.",
      "meta_description": ""
    },
