  {
    "council_member": "Mike Renaud",
    "council_position": "President and Chief Executive Officer",
    "organization": "Valle del Sol",
    "website": "https://www.valledelsol.com",
    "about": {
      "about_url": "https://www.valledelsol.com/about/",
      "mission": "Our work is rooted in compassion, equity, and community empowerment:",
      "description": "Learn about Valle Del Sol Community Health, a nonprofit FQHC serving Phoenix and Mesa since 1970, founded by civil rights activists. Contact us to learn more! ",
      "raw_text": "Valle Del Sol Community Health is a federally qualified health center (FQHC) and nonprofit community health organization dedicated to transforming lives across the greater Phoenix Valley. For more than 50 years, we've provided integrated medical and behavioral health services to adults, children, seniors, and families from all backgrounds.\n\nWe offer comprehensive care under one roof: primary care, pediatrics, women's health, behavioral health, substance use recovery, psychiatry, and wellness services. Our team delivers culturally centered, bilingual care that treats the whole person. We alsoaccept most insurance plansand offersliding-fee supportbased on income to ensure cost is not a barrier to care.\n\nWe provide care that honors the diverse traditions, languages, and experiences of the people we serve. Our English and Spanish speaking staff speak your language and understand our community, creating an environment where you can feel seen, heard, and respected.\n\nFrom the moment you walk through our doors, you'll experience person-centered care designed around your needs and your family's wellbeing. We believe in equitable access to services and offer comprehensive care regardless of your ability to pay, because your health should never depend on your income.\n\nCall us at(602) 258-6797or use ourpatient portalto get connected to our care across Phoenix, Mesa, and surrounding areas.\n\n**This health center receives HHS funding and has Federal Public Health Service (PHS) deemed status with respect to certain health or health-related claims, including medical malpractice claims, for itself and its covered individuals.\n\nOur work is rooted in compassion, equity, and community empowerment:\n\nThese principles guide every interaction, every service, and every decision we make. They reflect our commitment to preserving the dignity of all people while creating the standards by which others are measured.\n\nValle Del Sol Community Health was founded in 1970 by social justice activists who saw a critical gap in behavioral health and social support services for Latino and underserved communities in Phoenix. What began as a civil rights organization has grown into a trusted leader in integrated healthcare, rooted in the belief that everyone deserves compassionate, culturally aligned care. For over five decades, we've listened to our community and evolved our services to meet their needs, from adding youth services in the mid-70s to incorporating primary care in 2011.\n\nToday, we operate multiple clinics throughout the Phoenix metropolitan area and continue to innovate. OurHispanic Leadership Instituteempowers the next generation of diverse leaders, and our annualProfiles of Success Hispanic Leadership Awards Dinnercelebrates Latino leadership across Arizona—making us more than a health center, but a true community anchor.\n\nValle Del Sol Community Health is guided by an executive team deeply committed to our mission and immersed in the communities we serve. Our leaders bring decades of experience in healthcare, community advocacy, and organizational excellence, ensuring Valle Del Sol Community Health remains responsive to community needs while maintaining the highest standards of care.\n\nThey lead with authentic empathy, honoring our civil rights legacy while driving innovation across our growing network of clinics throughout the Phoenix metropolitan area.Meet the Team Behind Valle Del Sol Community Health",
      "meta_description": "Valle Del Sol Community Health offers integrative and comprehensive  medical care and health services in Phoenix and Mesa. Keep your entire family healthy with services ranging from primary care to behavioral health under one roof. Contact us today! "
    },
