    "organization": "Terros Health",
    "website": "https://www.terroshealth.org",
    "about": {
      "about_url": "https://www.terroshealth.org",
      "mission": "",
      "description": "Terros Health — making healthcare more accessible and affordable for all.",
      "raw_text": "Comprehensive Care with a Personal Touch.\n\nAt Terros Health, we are a team united in a desire to help patients become the best versions of themselves while creating healthy communities. We foster a culture where our team members feel seen, supported and appreciated, so every person we serve receives that same level of compassion and respect.\n\nEveryone deserves access to quality health care. It’s why we meet people where they are — virtually, in the community or at our health and counseling centers across the Valley and throughout the state. Walk-ins are always welcome. Once patients are here, we leave no stone unturned in helping them get comprehensive, compassionate care.\n\nCheck out the latest news about Terros Health and stay up-to-date on all that’s happening at Terros Health bysubscribingto our monthly newsletter.\n\nFind out how we are living our mission of serving others at work and in the community.\n\nJoin us for our 2nd annual Hope, Health & Healing Brunch",
      "meta_description": "Terros Health — making healthcare more accessible and affordable for all."
    },
    "team": {
      "team_url": "https://terroshealth.org/leadership-team/",
      "members": [
        {
          "name": "Executive Team",
          "role": "Dr. Karen Hoffman TepperPresident and Chief Executive OfficerClick to view biography",
          "photo_url": "https://terroshealth.org/wp-content/uploads/2025/08/dr-karen-tepper.webp",
          "bio": "Providing high quality, accessible care for those most in need within a system that is complex, fragmented and often broken is more than a job, it is a passion. Equally important to Dr. Karen Hoffman Tepper is the responsibility to care for the caregivers, “our employees who work so hard are heroes and it is my job to support them in their very important work.”",
          "local_photo": "photos/Terros_Health/Executive_Team.webp"
        }
      ]
    },
